.TH "INSPEKT" "1" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inspekt \- browser inspection, accessibility testing, and automation
from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] [\f[I]GLOBAL OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]COMMAND\f[R]
[\f[I]ARGS\f[R]]\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] is a command\-line companion for a real, running
browser.
It connects to a browser extension (Chrome, Firefox, Safari) or an
isolated Chromium running inside the Inspekt VM, and exposes that
session as a rich set of subcommands: navigate, click and type, run
accessibility audits, extract content, take screenshots, record and
replay flows, query the DOM, drive plugins, and expose everything to AI
agents over MCP.
.PP
Most commands operate on the \f[I]currently focused\f[R] browser tab.
Use the global \f[B]\(eninstance\f[R] option to target a specific
browser instance by its short ID, alias, or zero\-based index.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enversion\f[R]
Show the version and exit.
.TP
\f[B]\-v\f[R], \f[B]\(enverbose\f[R]
Enable verbose output (timing, requests, state changes)
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-tips\f[R]
Suppress tips and hints in output
.TP
\f[B]\-i\f[R], \f[B]\(eninstance\f[R], \f[I]ID\f[R]
Target specific browser instance by ID, alias, or index (e.g.,
\(lqb7x2\(rq, \(lqhomepage\(rq, \(lq0\(rq)
